From: WinBoat
Subject: [PATCH] d3d9umd, d3d10umd, wgl: the user-mode drivers on Windows 7

Windows 7 (the kernel driver's WDDM 1.1 build) didn't load the drivers or used Windows 8 interfaces they then lacked:
- util/futex: WaitOnAddress and WakeByAddress* are Windows 8's (an import every driver had: none loaded, 0x8007007F):
  looked up in kernelbase, else a condition variable per address bucket (a waiter checks the value under the bucket's
  lock, a waker takes it to wake the bucket's waiters)
- gdikmt_create_from_luid: no D3DKMTOpenAdapterFromLuid: the enumerated adapter with the LUID (Direct3D 9 had no HAL)
- d3d9umd: the runtime's (interface 0x2003) device function table ends before Windows 8's entries (VolBlt1 on): only
  that much written, and CreateResource, Flush, Present and the Tex/Vol/BufBlt it calls kept (Windows 8 and later
  still get them cleared for their 1/2 versions)
- d3d9umd, d3d10umd: the device callbacks end before Windows 8's (SignalSynchronizationObject2Cb on): what follows them
  in the copy zeroed (a call through it jumped to the runtime's version number, 0x2003); the completion events then go
  through gdi32's D3DKMTSignalSynchronizationObject2 (gdikmt_signal_cpu_event, WGL's path too), which on Windows 7
  can't enqueue a CPU event: the event is set at once (the host runs all contexts' work in submission order and the
  CPU's reads wait for their resources, so only the CPU's frame pacing is lost)
---
diff --git a/src/gallium/auxiliary/gdikmt/gdikmt.h b/src/gallium/auxiliary/gdikmt/gdikmt.h
index 0cc1af4..15d1bba 100644
--- a/src/gallium/auxiliary/gdikmt/gdikmt.h
+++ b/src/gallium/auxiliary/gdikmt/gdikmt.h
@@ -116,6 +116,12 @@ gdikmt_wddm2_make_resident(struct gdikmt_wddm2_residency *residency, const struc
  * (Windows 8.1) the desktop's displays' adapters. Returns how many */
 UINT gdikmt_enum_adapters(D3DKMT_ADAPTERINFO *adapters, UINT max);
 
+/* Windows 7: the D3D runtimes' callbacks end before Windows 8's (SignalSynchronizationObject2Cb on) */
+bool gdikmt_windows7(void);
+/* A CPU event set once the context's work so far is done, through gdi32 (for runtimes without the callback); set
+ * at once where the kernel can't (Windows 7) */
+NTSTATUS gdikmt_signal_cpu_event(D3DKMT_HANDLE hContext, HANDLE event);
+
 struct gdikmt_device *gdikmt_create_from_hdc(HDC hDC);
 /* Opens the adapter with this LUID through the D3DKMT* functions */
 struct gdikmt_device *gdikmt_create_from_luid(LUID luid);
diff --git a/src/gallium/auxiliary/gdikmt/gdikmt_d3dkmt.c b/src/gallium/auxiliary/gdikmt/gdikmt_d3dkmt.c
index b3218bd..8fe60ec 100644
--- a/src/gallium/auxiliary/gdikmt/gdikmt_d3dkmt.c
+++ b/src/gallium/auxiliary/gdikmt/gdikmt_d3dkmt.c
